{"task_id": "HumanEval/98", "solution": "def count_upper(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string s, count the number of uppercase vowels in even indices.\n    \n    For example:\n    count_upper('aBCdEf') returns 1\n    count_upper('abcdefg') returns 0\n    count_upper('dBBE') returns 0\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    # Define the default set of uppercase vowels as per design context.\n    uppercase_vowels = {'A', 'E', 'I', 'O', 'U'}\n\n    # Iterate through the string, considering only even indices.\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 2):\n        char = s[i]\n        # Check if the character is an uppercase vowel.\n        if char in uppercase_vowels:\n            count += 1\n            \n    return count"}
